{"kind":"assert","text":"U1 (ea7faed9): a read of main before building finds the note's step 1 larger than \"a new rules definition\", and five points need your ruling. First commit fbbad39d (note approved) is done; I build nothing more until you answer.\n\nFacts (read at eae5ce3b):\nF1. A room's Rules pin comes from its Directory (SIBLINGS_OF, packages/platform/src/directory.ts:80), and its Directory from its Register (register.ts:57). U1 therefore needs a new creation family: Register 29, Directory 28, Rules 16 (Membership 14, Destination 21 unchanged), with the version-relations, native-catalog, version-questions, reader pin lists, archive-policy rows, generated declarations and four seals that follow.\nF2. Only the entry that opens an item may write a fixed slot (packages/derive/src/effects.ts:284). Rules 16 must make release and presentation non-fixed; no per-act exemption exists.\nF3. The installation item's uri names the commit, and MCP reads uri (packages/mcp/src/service.ts:356). An in-place upgrade must change uri too, beyond the note's \"release and presentation only\".\nF4. An item holds at most 12 values (packages/contract/src/definition.ts:97); installation already has 12. A replaces ref fits (refs: 3 of 12).\nF5. APPLICATION_TRUST exists only on the host; a pure rule cannot read it. The host prepares a fetch only for an install-application intent (packages/scope/src/applications/outside.ts:32). The trust check therefore runs as a fetch-application outcome: the act opens the fetch, and the confirmed answer applies the in-place change; a refused answer (untrusted-release) changes nothing. outside.ts (not sealed) must accept upgrade-application.\n\nDecisions, with my recommendation:\nD1. In place changes uri, release and presentation (F3). Recommend yes.\nD2. A changed publisher is refused in both forms, not only in place. Recommend yes.\nD3. When item N ends in the replace form: at the act (the note), or in the successor's creation entry. At the act, a refused successor leaves no active Counter; at creation, never two active and never none, but the archive stop position moves (U2). Recommend at creation.\nD4. Red (d) \"a second active Counter cannot result\" covers upgrade-application only. A plain install-application of the same app can still make two (IR-1); \"same application\" needs a definition and no value slot is free. Recommend: U1 scopes red (d) to the upgrade act; a later request decides the install guard.\nD5. U1 is a new creation family (F1), so U1 needs no new Membership but does need a Register; U4's witness room uses it via PLATFORM_CREATION_PINS. Recommend: accept the family in U1.\nCoupling: do not deploy U1 to a room that archives before U2 (in-place items stop matching birth identifiers: hourly retry). No new alarm; each upgrade costs one fetch operation, as an install does.","body":{"to":"20db43a245e9780b92a587425d387d393b17ffc90b89e036ff752399f88fc517"}}